l-projection | literal invocation selector | selector | equals selection.selector | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-initiator-selector-mismatch</code> |\n12312|| logs | initiator | initial-projection | alias of selected source | source_alias | equals selected source alias (null for local) | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-initiator-alias-mismatch</code> |\n12313|| logs | initiator | initial-projection | resolved session UUID | session_id | equals resolved session_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-initiator-session-mismatch</code> |\n12314|| logs | initiator | initial-projection | resolved record digest | session_record_id | equals resolved session_record_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-initiator-record-mismatch</code> |\n12315|| logs | initiator | initial-projection | resolved source host | source_host_id | equals resolved source_host_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-initiator-source-mismatch</code> |\n12316|| logs | initiator | cursor-projection | route logs with cursor | action | equals logs | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-initiator-action-mismatch</code> |\n12317|| logs | initiator | cursor-projection | explicit --peer host with cursor | destination_host_id | equals peer_host | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-initiator-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12318|| logs | initiator | cursor-projection | literal invocation selector | selector | equals selection.selector | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-initiator-selector-mismatch</code> |\n12319|| logs | initiator | cursor-projection | alias of selected source | source_alias | equals selected source alias (null for local) | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-initiator-alias-mismatch</code> |\n12320|| logs | initiator | cursor-projection | resolved session UUID | session_id | equals resolved session_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-initiator-session-mismatch</code> |\n12321|| logs | initiator | cursor-projection | resolved record digest | session_record_id | equals resolved session_record_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-initiator-record-mismatch</code> |\n12322|| logs | initiator | cursor-projection | resolved source host | source_host_id | equals resolved source_host_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-initiator-source-mismatch</code> |\n12323|| logs | receiver | initial-projection | resolved session UUID | session_id | equals resolved session_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-receiver-session-mismatch</code> |\n12324|| logs | receiver | initial-projection | resolved record digest | session_record_id | equals resolved session_record_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-receiver-record-mismatch</code> |\n12325|| logs | receiver | initial-projection | route logs | action | equals logs | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-receiver-action-mismatch</code> |\n12326|| logs | receiver | initial-projection | explicit --peer host | destination_host_id | equals peer_host per-endpoint | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-receiver-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12327|| logs | receiver | cursor-projection | resolved session UUID | session_id | equals resolved session_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-receiver-session-mismatch</code> |\n12328|| logs | receiver | cursor-projection | resolved record digest | session_record_id | equals resolved session_record_id | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-receiver-record-mismatch</code> |\n12329|| logs | receiver | cursor-projection | route logs with cursor | action | equals logs | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-receiver-action-mismatch</code> |\n12330|| logs | receiver | cursor-projection | explicit --peer host with cursor | destination_host_id | equals peer_host per-endpoint | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-receiver-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12331|| logs | both | initial-projection | route logs | action | both equal logs | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-both-action-mismatch</code> |\n12332|| logs | both | initial-projection | explicit --peer host | destination_host_id | both equal peer_host | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-both-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12333|| logs | both | cursor-projection | route logs with cursor | action | both equal logs | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-both-action-mismatch</code> |\n12334|| logs | both | cursor-projection | explicit --peer host with cursor | destination_host_id | both equal peer_host | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-both-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12335|\n12336|Other managed-session remote action routes use Section 11's existing typed\n12337|session_id and LeaseExpectation/transaction IDs; they MUST carry the selected\n12338|UUID and existing expected authority, never convert either into a CLI NAME.\n12339|Their closed RPC envelopes and bound error versions are unchanged. Selector\n12340|failures are emitted locally as CLI5/Error1.4, not inserted into an older RPC.\n12341|\n12342|#### 14.7.3 Authoritative summaries and closed failure binding\n12343|\n12344|Selector-capable CLI defaults to CLI Result 5.0.0 and Structured Error 1.4.0.\n12345|Explicit <code>--result-version VERSION</code> selects a supported exact CLI\n12346|Result version before parsing command operands; unsupported versions fail locally\n12347|with incompatible_schema. Version 5 retains the exact v4 success envelope,\n12348|command/body registry and SessionSummary shape. It changes selector admission and\n12349|requires authoritative projection below. A canceled chooser emits the selected\n12350|record's existing NAME in the unchanged cancel body, not the qualified argument.\n12351|There is no successful public incomplete-session variant and no nullable owner,\n12352|lease epoch zero, synthetic lease ID, or added SessionState.\n12353|\n12354|Every SessionSummary owner_host_id, lease_epoch and lease_id comes from the\n12355|validated winning Lease Record, including the initial epoch-1 create lease.\n12356|owner_host_name comes from validated host metadata for that holder; missing host\n12357|metadata is a refusal, never the source alias. local_role compares that holder\n12358|with the local host UUID. Before the first checkpoint, both newest-checkpoint\n12359|members are null; creating is valid only with an authoritative initial lease\n12360|and the existing eligible-bootstrap facts. A Session Record alone proves\n12361|identity/provenance, not creation of an owner or a creating lifecycle. Liveness\n12362|and capabilities require the existing observation/evidence contracts; source\n12363|reachability, a cached row or an absent observation cannot mint process_present,\n12364|readiness, capability, or current ownership. An unknown required observation is\n12365|selector_observation_unavailable. Read-only inspection never creates a lease.\n12366|\n12367|A complete read proving a record without any valid lease returns\n12368|selector_bootstrap_incomplete; a failed read follows the local/remote read classification above,\n12369|and corrupt/inconsistent authority returns integrity_failure/lease_conflict as\n12370|applicable. List refuses the whole success document if an encountered record\n12371|cannot be represented truthfully; it MUST NOT silently omit that record, invent\n12372|summary fields, or use partial/unreachable_peer_ids to conceal a record-only\n12373|bootstrap. Existing legitimate peer-partial list semantics otherwise remain.\n12374|\n12375|Structured Error 1.4.0 keeps the exact 1.3 top-level shape and all earlier\n12376|code-to-exit mappings and adds exactly:\n12377|\n12378|| Exit | Code | Required meaning |\n12379|| ---: | --- | --- |\n12380|| 4 | <code>selector_source_not_found</code> | Complete valid config has no requested source |\n12381|| 8 | <code>selector_source_read_failed</code> | Remote source transport/I/O read failed; no fallback; local I/O uses local_precondition_failed and partial/malformed evidence uses integrity_failure |\n12382|| 12 | <code>selector_bootstrap_incomplete</code> | Complete authority read proves record-only creation; inspect/recover original bootstrap |\n12383|| 3 | <code>selector_observation_unavailable</code> | Required summary observation or host metadata cannot be established |\n12384|| 16 | <code>selector_plan_stale</code> | Bound selection facts changed; fresh plan/confirmation required |\n12385|\n12386|These five errors have retryable=false; known session/operation IDs are included.\n12387|Redacted details may explain phase/source without secrets or inventing facts.\n12388|Only CLI Result 5 binds Error 1.4; selector errors MUST NOT be emitted inside\n12389|legacy RPC/Provider/Directory envelopes. CLI Result 1/2/3/4 retain exact historical\n12390|syntax, body and Error 1.0/1.1/1.2/1.3 bindings respectively. An explicitly selected\n12391|legacy result version refuses id:/qualified selector syntax with its bound\n12392|invalid_arguments, never silently treats it as a name. Unrepresentable summaries\n12393|on legacy surfaces refuse with that surface's existing local_precondition_failed\n12394|(exit 3); incompatible_schema covers unsupported representation versions.\n12395|No lower-version successful projection may fabricate missing authority. Record,\n12396|lease, event and error objects already published are never rewritten/re-digested.\n12397|\n12398|#### 14.7.4 Interrupted record-only creation\n12399|\n12400|The crash gap inside Section 13.1 step 2 (Session Record durable, initial Lease\n12401|Record not yet durable) is recovery work, before creating. Recovery runs only on\n12402|the original creating host under a serialized machine-local BootstrapIntent\n12403|and its original operation IDs. Selector contract 1.0.0 defines this closed\n12404|local representation: selector_version (exact 1.0.0), session_record_id (digest),\n12405|workspace_group_record_id (digest), creating_host_id (UUIDv7),\n12406|bootstrap_operation_id (UUIDv7), first_checkpoint_operation_id (UUIDv7), and\n12407|initial_lease (the complete allocated Lease Record 1.0.0 described by the\n12408|closed bootstrap representation table below).\n12409|New creation MUST atomically persist and fsync this intent and its parent\n12410|directory before publishing the Session Record. Retain it through durable\n12411|session.created publication and reconcile against immutable authority on retry.\n12412|It is never replicated, never a lease grant, and never accepted from caller\n12413|bytes as recovery authority. Its encoding is canonical JSON under selector\n12414|contract 1.0.0, not an extension of a historical journal. Legacy record-only\n12415|creation without this original intent remains refused; no migration invents it. It requires a complete valid authority read proving no lease,\n12416|no terminal/provider effect and no conflicting creation; an unavailable read\n12417|cannot establish any of those absences. It reuses the already allocated/persisted\n12418|initial lease and operation IDs, validates the Session Record/Workspace Group,\n12419|and durably publishes the initial epoch-1 create lease and session.created in the\n12420|original order before any terminal/provider action. The same intent ordering\n12421|applies to task-board creation in Section 13.2 step 1. If the original durable\n12422|bootstrap inputs are missing, ambiguous or inconsistent, remain refused with\n12423|selector_bootstrap_incomplete for manual diagnosis; do not allocate replacement\n12424|IDs, infer the creator is owner, recover from another peer, or launch a second\n12425|process. When the lease already exists, reconcile it and the original intent;\n12426|never issue a second initial lease. A lease/event read failure is not the\n12427|record-only case. Normal Section 13.1 bootstrap retry begins only after these\n12428|facts are established. No new recovery command, replicated journal schema, or\n12429|cross-host create authority is introduced.\n12430|\n12431|The exact BootstrapIntent members are the seven members above, all required;\n12432|unknown members are refused. Its embedded Lease Record retains every required\n12433|Section 5.3 member, including nullable members, canonical self digest,\n12434|UUIDv4 fencing token, timestamp and reverse-DNS extensions. The following\n12435|initial-lease values and cross-record bindings are normative, and are consumed\n12436|by the publication evaluator in addition to structural validation:\n12437|\n12438|| Bootstrap constraint | Required value |\n12439|| --- | --- |\n12440|| epoch | 1 |\n12441|| reason | create |\n12442|| predecessor_lease_id | null |\n12443|| checkpoint_id | null |\n12444|| schema | urn:ax:schema:lease |\n12445|| schema_version | 1.0.0 |\n12446|\n12447|Intent session_record_id and workspace_group_record_id must equal the canonical\n12448|record digests of the supplied Session/Workspace Group. Session subject_id equals\n12449|session_id; Workspace Group subject_id equals workspace_group_id; the Session's\n12450|workspace_group_id equals that group's ID and its launch cwd names a member.\n12451|Lease session_id and subject_id equal the Session ID. Intent creating_host_id,\n12452|Session created_by_host_id, lease holder_host_id, issued_by_host_id and\n12453|created_by_host_id equal the original creating host and the recovering local\n12454|host. An existing reused Workspace Group need not have the same creator.\n12455|Both operation IDs are distinct UUIDv7 and equal the IDs in the original durable\n12456|creation inputs; initial_lease is byte-identical after canonicalization to the\n12457|originally allocated lease. Recovery compares the whole original intent, not\n12458|just its digest, against trusted machine-local original inputs. Rehashed caller\n12459|records, fresh operation IDs or a fresh valid lease cannot replace them.\n12460|Absent or malformed original intent, invalid embedded lease, or inconsistent\n12461|bindings refuse selector_bootstrap_incomplete before publication. A failed read\n12462|of those inputs retains its read-failure class, not absence. Existing-lease\n12463|reconciliation first validates the same intent and must not republish a lease.\n12464|The original-input provenance, serialization, effect absence and complete\n12465|observation checks remain runtime prerequisites; concrete synthetic record\n12466|validation does not prove those runtime facts.\n12467|\n12468|#### 14.7.5 Publication conformance and assurance bounds\n12469|\n12470|The following closed machine-readable policy is normative for the selector\n12471|reference evaluator in the publication gate. The policy is the executable normative admission/refusal representation for\n12472|the eight listed source-conformance families. The guard expression grammar is\n12473|closed: get reads a required context field; eq/ne compare JSON values; gt\n12474|compares counts; all/any combine booleans. Guard lists evaluate in order and\n12475|refuse with the first matching error. Missing fields, unknown operators/stages,\n12476|or malformed policy are publication failures. Prose explains these predicates\n12477|and additionally specifies runtime authority/durability obligations outside the\n12478|source evaluator. Prose and policy must agree; neither\n12479|synthetic vectors nor source fingerprints prove a running AX implementation.\n12480|The fixture families below are the independently enumerated publication scope.\n12481|\n12482|| ID | Publication obligation |\n12483|| --- | --- |\n12484|| SEL-GRAMMAR | First-at grammar, exact aliases, explicit durable UUIDs and input bounds |\n12485|| SEL-PRECEDENCE | Bare tier order, collisions and tombstones |\n12486|| SEL-SOURCE | Missing/read-failed/empty source and no explicit-source fallback |\n12487|| SEL-PLAN | Resolve once and all bound facts revalidated before effects |\n12488|| SEL-AUTHORITY | Source is neither owner nor destination |\n12489|| SEL-SUMMARY | Initial lease/observation projection and truthful refusal |\n12490|| SEL-BOOTSTRAP | Interrupted record-only recovery with original durable inputs |\n12491|| SEL-VERSION | Exact versions and closed historical behavior |\n12492|\n12493|\n12494|The exact source-only case inventory is closed; dropping a case is a publication\n12495|failure, not a reduction of the denominator.\n12496|\n12497|Publication composition derives its action/boundary and SelectionPlan member\n12498|inventory from Section 14.7.2, including both CLI5 remote routes. Each endpoint\n12499|inherits the action boundaries except the opposite transport endpoint:\n12500|remote-admission belongs to the receiver, remote-dispatch to the initiator.\n12501|Session-filtered logs require separate initial and cursor-continuation witnesses.\n12502|Every resulting row requires an unchanged positive, revoked and forged-plan\n12503|negatives, failed/partial/malformed reads in each local/remote domain, and one\n12504|changed and one missing current-fact witness for every bound SelectionPlan member.\n12505|The opposite endpoint remains valid. These synthetic vectors must execute the\n12506|composed publication evaluator, not only generic revalidation. Caller and generic\n12507|checks must independently resist scope narrowing. Recovery is measured for the\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c703","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08841-b416-7e52-96f7-950fb1e6ed56"},"sequence":476,"recorded_at":1780531400000947,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08842-838a-7a13-8d98-315f3b3aff18"},"task_id":"01a08842-838a-7a13-8d98-315f3b3aff18","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a08842-838a-7a13-8d98-315f3b3aff18"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c705","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08841-b416-7e52-96f7-950fb1e6ed56"},"sequence":477,"recorded_at":1780531400000949,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f"},"call_id":"call_01a088427f9c7c52b592d9bf9b6a50eb","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(11867 line(s) above)\n11868|### 14.7 Session selector 1.0.0 and CLI Result 5.0.0\n11869|\n11870|This section is the v0.6.0 selector contract. It applies to the umbrella\n11871|<code>ax SELECTOR</code> and every existing managed-session NAME operand in\n11872|Section 14, including status, attach, takeover, fork, stop, resume, sync,\n11873|diff, materialize, logs --session and session set-profile. Creation NAME, destination HOST,\n11874|provider-native identifiers, Directory instance IDs/query expressions, and the\n11875|internal <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code> are not selector operands. No new\n11876|product operation or ownership authority is introduced.\n11877|\n11878|#### 14.7.1 Literal grammar and source-index resolution\n11879|\n11880|A selector is one CLI argument. Ordinary shell quoting handles spaces; the CLI\n11881|MUST NOT join multiple arguments, expand aliases as shell text, decode percent\n11882|escapes, normalize Unicode, trim, or case-fold configured host aliases. Split\n11883|at the FIRST literal <code>@</code> only. The key is either a Section 2 session\n11884|NAME or <code>id:SESSION_UUID</code>, with a canonical lowercase UUIDv7; neither\n11885|key form contains <code>@</code>. A bare UUID retains Section 2.3 name-first\n11886|precedence. <code>id:</code> explicitly bypasses names and never denotes a\n11887|provider-native ID, directory instance ID, lease ID, or UUID prefix.\n11888|\n11889|| Form | Meaning |\n11890|| --- | --- |\n11891|| <code>NAME</code> / bare UUID | Exact Section 2.3 local-name, peer-name, UUID, not-found precedence; collision refusal unchanged |\n11892|| <code>id:SESSION_UUID</code> | Durable AX session UUID in the local and allowed-peer union, independent of names |\n11893|| <code>KEY@local</code> | Only the local derived source index |\n11894|| <code>KEY@peer:ALIAS</code> | Only the configured peer source whose entire remaining suffix is the literal alias |\n11895|| <code>KEY@id:HOST_UUID</code> | Only the source whose canonical host UUID is given; local UUID selects local; otherwise exactly one allowlisted configured peer |\n11896|\n11897|Examples: <code>ax status build@local</code>,\n11898|<code>ax status build@peer:workstation</code>,\n11899|<code>ax status \"build@peer:Work Laptop\"</code>,\n11900|<code>ax status \"build@peer:Ops@east:თბილისი\"</code>, and\n11901|<code>ax status id:0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab</code>.\n11902|A percent sign in an alias is literal. <code>peer:</code> with an empty alias,\n11903|unknown source prefixes, malformed durable IDs, and an empty key are invalid\n11904|arguments. The alias obeys the existing configured name bound, 1–64 characters;\n11905|this grammar adds no alias encoding, normalization, or registration path.\n11906|\n11907|Resolution first validates configuration, including uniqueness of exact alias\n11908|and host-ID mappings. Duplicate source mappings are invalid_config, never\n11909|first-match selection. An explicit unknown alias/host is selector_source_not_found;\n11910|a known but disallowed peer is peer_not_allowlisted. A failed, partial, malformed,\n11911|or inaccessible config read is invalid_config. A remote source transport/I/O read failure is selector_source_read_failed\n11912|(exit 8); a local source/store I/O failure is the existing\n11913|local_precondition_failed (exit 3). A partial or malformed index/authority\n11914|response is integrity_failure (exit 9), not absence. A complete valid empty index\n11915|or a complete index without the selected live key returns not_found. A malformed\n11916|record or digest failure is integrity_failure. These outcomes MUST remain distinct.\n11917|An explicit source MUST NOT fall back to the local index, another peer, a cached\n11918|index from another source, or a union search, even when the same name/UUID exists\n11919|there. A peer source requires a complete read of that peer's advertised index\n11920|under the selected transport, with verified configured host identity; a local\n11921|cached observation does not prove that read succeeded.\n11922|\n11923|For a qualified NAME, select in that source only: exact live name first, then\n11924|exact UUID if the NAME is UUID-shaped. Deduplicate multiple copies of the same\n11925|session UUID only when their immutable record digest agrees. Distinct live\n11926|UUIDs with the same name or ASCII-fold-colliding names return name_ambiguous.\n11927|For bare input retain exactly Section 2.3 tiers: a local exact match wins over a\n11928|peer exact match; a peer exact match wins over UUID interpretation. Collision\n11929|checks apply within the reached tier. Unread lower tiers need not be consulted\n11930|after a unique higher-tier match. A tier that must be read but cannot be read\n11931|is a read failure, not permission to proceed to a lower tier. Tombstoned entries\n11932|are excluded only with authoritative tombstone evidence, not a failed record read.\n11933|\n11934|#### 14.7.2 Resolve once, bind facts, revalidate execution\n11935|\n11936|Resolve the key to a session UUID once per invocation/confirmed plan. Build a\n11937|machine-local immutable SelectionPlan under selector contract 1.0.0 with exactly\n11938|the required members in this table. No plan hash, name, source, or display field\n11939|is a capability. A persisted plan has a locally verified canonical digest over\n11940|all members; caller-supplied digest equality alone is not evidence of authority.\n11941|\n11942|| Member | Type and binding |\n11943|| --- | --- |\n11944|| <code>selector_version</code> | Exact 1.0.0 |\n11945|| <code>selector</code> | Original single argument, at most 134 characters (64-character NAME + @ + peer: + 64-character alias) |\n11946|| <code>session_id</code> | Selected UUIDv7, never resolved again by name |\n11947|| <code>session_record_id</code> | Validated immutable Session Record digest for that UUID |\n11948|| <code>source_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 of the selected source; for a bare union match, provenance host of the selected entry, deterministic bytewise host-ID tie break for identical copies |\n11949|| <code>source_alias</code> | Exact configured alias or null for local; a diagnostic label, never identity |\n11950|| <code>source_index_digest</code> | Digest of the complete validated index read used for selection |\n11951|| <code>configuration_digest</code> | Digest of effective validated configuration, including peer mapping, allowlist and selected transport |\n11952|| <code>lease_record_id</code> | Validated winning Lease Record digest |\n11953|| <code>lease_epoch</code>, <code>lease_id</code>, <code>owner_host_id</code> | Positive uint53, UUIDv4, UUIDv7, all from that same winning lease |\n11954|| <code>authority_heads</code> | Sorted unique digest array of the validated lease/event/tombstone heads used for the decision |\n11955|| <code>action</code> | Explicit existing command/action tag selected under Sections 2.3 and 14 |\n11956|| <code>destination_host_id</code> | Explicit destination UUIDv7 or null when action has no destination; independently validated |\n11957|| <code>expectation_digest</code> | Digest binding the action's existing checkpoint/workspace/cohort/provider/terminal/confirmation expectations; does not replace those contracts |\n11958|\n11959|A source is an index location, never destination or proof of current ownership.\n11960|A local source can describe a remote owner; a peer source can describe a local\n11961|owner. Summary owner/role and execution routing MUST use the validated winning\n11962|lease and local-host comparison, never the source host or Session Record creator.\n11963|\n11964|Immediately before any effect, and again at every existing fencing/commit/retry\n11965|boundary, reread current configuration and required source data, validate the\n11966|same immutable Session Record, current tombstones and complete authority union,\n11967|winning lease and action prerequisites. Compare every bound plan fact. A changed\n11968|mapping, alias, allowlist, transport, source index, record, authority head, lease,\n11969|action, destination or expectation invalidates the plan. Return\n11970|selector_plan_stale before effects; explicit authorization revocation returns\n11971|peer_not_allowlisted; failed reads retain their read-failure classification.\n11972|Do not re-resolve by name, substitute a same-named session, silently replan,\n11973|transfer a lease, or reuse confirmation for new facts. An unrelated index change\n11974|may conservatively require a fresh plan. Reads revalidate before projecting output;\n11975|mutations retain existing serialized fencing/effect boundaries so a successful\n11976|precheck cannot authorize an effect after authority changes. If an earlier phase\n11977|already committed, use that operation's existing status/recovery contract with\n11978|its original IDs; a stale selection is not rollback or a new-operation retry.\n11979|\n11980|##### Selector execution boundaries\n11981|\n11982|The following action/boundary matrix is normative. Umbrella choices use their\n11983|selected action, never an umbrella bypass. `logs` applies when --session is\n11984|present; `cancel` only projects a choice. A boundary is reached only when the\n11985|existing operation reaches that phase; these rows do not introduce new effects.\n11986|`projection` precedes output, `pre-effect` precedes the first effect, `fencing`\n11987|covers every Section 5.3 fencing check, `commit` precedes durable publication,\n11988|`retry` and `recovery` precede continuation using original operation IDs.\n11989|`remote-dispatch` precedes sending attach expectations, `remote-admission`\n11990|precedes owner input, and `transport-resume` covers reconnect or sleep/transport\n11991|interruption under Section 5.3. None may skip checks because a previous phase\n11992|succeeded. Post-commit recovery checks current authority without demanding that\n11993|an operation's own authorized committed transitions equal its pre-commit plan:\n11994|reconcile those transitions through the original operation's status/receipts,\n11995|then build and validate its continuation expectations before any further effect.\n11996|Unexpected transitions refuse; they never authorize a new operation.\n11997|\n11998|| Selector action | Required boundary classes |\n11999|| --- | --- |\n12000|| status | projection, retry |\n12001|| attach | pre-effect, fencing, retry, remote-dispatch, remote-admission, transport-resume |\n12002|| takeover | pre-effect, fencing, commit, retry, recovery, transport-resume |\n12003|| fork | pre-effect, fencing, commit, retry, recovery, transport-resume |\n12004|| stop | pre-effect, fencing, commit, retry, recovery, transport-resume |\n12005|| resume | pre-effect, fencing, commit, retry, recovery, transport-resume |\n12006|| sync | pre-effect, fencing, commit, retry, recovery, transport-resume |\n12007|| diff | projection, retry |\n12008|| materialize | pre-effect, fencing, commit, retry, recovery |\n12009|| session.set-profile | pre-effect, fencing, commit, retry, recovery |\n12010|| logs | projection, retry, remote-dispatch, remote-admission, transport-resume |\n12011|| cancel | projection |\n12012|\n12013|##### CLI 5 remote attach route\n12014|\n12015|For CLI Result 5 only, this paragraph supersedes the NAME forwarding and\n12016|re-resolution in Sections 13.4–13.5. The initiating host revalidates its complete\n12017|SelectionPlan at remote-dispatch, then invokes the argv-equivalent of:\n12018|\n12019|~~~shell\n12020|ssh -t HOST ax attach id:SESSION_UUID --local --result-version 5.0.0 --expect-selection EXPECTATIONS_JSON\n12021|~~~\n12022|\n12023|HOST is the verified configured endpoint for the plan's winning owner, never\n12024|the source. EXPECTATIONS_JSON is one canonically encoded JSON argument with\n12025|exactly the members/types in the following table. Transport invocation MUST\n12026|preserve argument boundaries with platform-appropriate shell quoting; no alias,\n12027|name or JSON value may become executable shell text. No application input is\n12028|forwarded until remote-admission succeeds. The selected configured transport\n12029|and its authentication/host-verification requirements remain mandatory; this\n12030|route does not weaken any stronger host-channel requirement or introduce an\n12031|RPC method. If that transport cannot carry the owner CLI attach stream with\n12032|its required authentication, refuse capability_unavailable before dispatch;\n12033|never downgrade to another transport. The receiver must support exact CLI 5;\n12034|an unsupported version refuses incompatible_schema, never retries legacy NAME\n12035|or bare UUID. CLI 1–4 retain the historical route and closed bytes.\n12036|\n12037|| Attach expectation | Type |\n12038|| --- | --- |\n12039|| selector_version | Exact 1.0.0 |\n12040|| session_id | UUIDv7 |\n12041|| session_record_id | digest |\n12042|| lease_record_id | digest |\n12043|| lease_epoch | Positive uint53 |\n12044|| lease_id | UUIDv4 |\n12045|| owner_host_id | UUIDv7 |\n12046|| authority_heads | digest array |\n12047|| expectation_digest | digest |\n12048|\n12049|These are expected values, not caller authentication or a capability. The\n12050|receiver validates them against its independently read exact session, winning\n12051|lease, complete authority and attach prerequisites; it uses a local plan with\n12052|its own source/configuration facts. The initiator's configuration digest or\n12053|source alias is never substituted for the receiver's local configuration.\n12054|Unknown/missing/extra expectation members or a non-id operand with this flag\n12055|are invalid_arguments; well-formed changed expectations are selector_plan_stale.\n12056|The flag is valid only for attach --local with CLI 5. A receiver that is not the\n12057|expected owner refuses selector_plan_stale rather than redirecting or taking\n12058|over. Both ends revalidate their own plans at their applicable boundaries.\n12059|Each end's plan action MUST equal attach and its destination MUST be null:\n12060|attach --local takes no destination argument, so a status plan, a plan for\n12061|another destination, or two agreeing copies of a wrong plan never authorize\n12062|attach input, even when that plan equals current. Two agreeing plan copies\n12063|prove nothing about the actual invocation.\n12064|The initiator plan MUST retain the literal single-argument selector and the\n12065|alias derived from the actually selected source (null for local): another\n12066|spelling that resolves to the same session UUID, or two agreeing copies of a\n12067|wrong selector/alias, never authorizes attach input. Receiver selector, alias\n12068|and source facts stay endpoint-local and are never cross-compared.\n12069|Receiver retry and transport-resume repeat exact-identity authority validation;\n12070|they never call NAME resolution. Receiver-local revocation/read/integrity\n12071|failures retain Section 14.7.1 classes and CLI 5/Error 1.4 binding. Caller\n12072|expectations cannot authorize input after revocation or a winning lease change.\n12073|\n12074|##### CLI 5 remote log filtering\n12075|\n12076|For CLI Result 5, the Section 14.1 remote logs NAME example and Result-1\n12077|validation are superseded by the following argv-equivalent. Resolve --session\n12078|once at the initiator and revalidate its plan before remote-dispatch. The\n12079|initiator refuses selector_plan_stale unless its plan session_id,\n12080|session_record_id and source_host_id equal the resolved selection;\n12081|plan/current agreement alone never proves selection binding:\n12082|\n12083|~~~shell\n12084|ssh HOST ax logs --session id:SESSION_UUID --limit N --json --result-version 5.0.0\n12085|~~~\n12086|\n12087|HOST is the explicit --peer log emitter, which may differ from both selection\n12088|source and winning owner. The receiver interprets id:SESSION_UUID as an exact\n12089|session-ID log filter, never a display name. It revalidates its local read plan\n12090|before projecting records; no ownership is granted and no record is created.\n12091|The initiating side validates exactly CLI Result 5 and the original command,\n12092|selected session filter, emitting_host_id and every returned event's host_id.\n12093|Session-scoped results contain only events for that exact session UUID. The\n12094|same Section 14.1 error classes, argument serialization, local-only remote\n12095|invocation and no-fan-out rules apply. Unsupported CLI5 refuses\n12096|incompatible_schema without retrying NAME, bare UUID or a lower result version.\n12097|A continuation cursor remains opaque to the initiator and is passed unchanged\n12098|to the same explicit --peer with --result-version 5.0.0. Its original durable\n12099|session filter is retained by the emitter; resume never re-resolves a name.\n12100|A cursor/emitter mismatch is invalid_arguments; forged emitter/event identity\n12101|is host_identity_mismatch/integrity_failure as in Section 14.1. Original plan\n12102|expectations must be revalidated at retry/transport-resume/projection boundaries.\n12103|Each end's plan action MUST equal logs. Each end's plan destination MUST equal\n12104|the actual explicit --peer host independently: the initiator's destination never\n12105|authorizes projection from another peer, and the receiver's destination is\n12106|checked against the same actual peer, never against the initiator's plan value.\n12107|A plan for another destination, or two ends agreeing on a wrong destination,\n12108|refuses selector_plan_stale. The initiator plan MUST retain the literal\n12109|--session selector and the alias derived from the actually selected source\n12110|(null for local) at every scope and boundary; another spelling resolving to\n12111|the same session, or two agreeing copies of a wrong selector/alias, refuses.\n12112|Source and configuration facts stay endpoint-local\n12113|and are never cross-compared. These bindings hold for initial and\n12114|cursor-continuation scopes and at every retry/resume boundary.\n12115|Historical CLI1–4 behavior stays closed and does not receive selector syntax.\n12116|\n12117|##### Composed invocation-to-plan binding\n12118|\n12119|\n12120|The composed routes bind every independent invocation/selection fact to each\n12121|endpoint plan exactly once per the following member disposition and relation.\n12122|Plan/current agreement\n12123|alone authorizes nothing: each divergence witness below keeps plan and current\n12124|in agreement while disagreeing with the actual invocation, and every witness\n12125|refuses selector_plan_stale. Cross-endpoint plan equality is never evidence;\n12126|trusted_local_plan marks a locally verified plan but never substitutes for\n12127|invocation binding. Receiver-local source and configuration facts keep the\n12128|meanings from the attach and logs paragraphs and are never cross-compared.\n12129|\n12130|Member disposition (all 16 SelectionPlan members; every member has exactly one\n12131|row; a new member without a row, or a new composed revalidation call site\n12132|without applicable rows, fails the publication gate closed rather than falling\n12133|into a default relation):\n12134|\n12135|| Plan member | Disposition | Independent fact and transformation, or endpoint-local evidence |\n12136|| --- | --- | --- |\n12137|| selector_version | endpoint-local observation | Constant 1.0.0; plan equals current via revalidate; no argv fact beyond version admission |\n12138|| selector | independent invocation fact (initiator only) | Initiator plan.selector equals the literal selection.selector single argument, even when another spelling resolves to the same UUID; receiver selector stays endpoint-local |\n12139|| session_id | independent invocation fact | Initiator plan.session_id equals resolved selection session_id; logs receiver plan.session_id equals the same resolved session_id; attach receiver session binds via expected lease admission plus revalidate, never via initiator equality; attach initiator session/record are jointly verified with owner exact-ID admission (a session-only divergence also changes the admitted record), logs isolates each clause |\n12140|| session_record_id | independent invocation fact | Same endpoints as session_id, against resolved session_record_id digest; same joint owner-admission note for attach, isolated caller narrowing on logs |\n12141|| source_host_id | independent invocation fact (initiator only) | Initiator plan.source_host_id equals resolved source_host_id; receiver source stays endpoint-local (valid distinct-source positives keep differing hosts) |\n12142|| source_alias | independent invocation fact (initiator only) | Initiator plan.source_alias equals the alias of the actually selected source (null for local); diagnostic label, never identity; receiver alias stays endpoint-local |\n12143|| source_index_digest | endpoint-local observation | Digest of the validated index read; no independent synthetic recomputation; plan equals current via revalidate; per-row changed/missing vectors |\n12144|| configuration_digest | endpoint-local observation | Digest of effective configuration; same evidence as source_index_digest |\n12145|| lease_record_id | endpoint-local observation | Winning lease digest; plan equals current via revalidate plus receiver expected admission; per-row vectors |\n12146|| lease_epoch | endpoint-local observation | Same evidence as lease_record_id |\n12147|| lease_id | endpoint-local observation | Same evidence as lease_record_id |\n12148|| owner_host_id | endpoint-local observation | Same evidence as lease_record_id; HOST derives from winning owner, never source |\n12149|| authority_heads | endpoint-local observation | Same evidence as lease_record_id |\n12150|| action | independent invocation fact (per endpoint) | Each end plan.action equals its actual route (attach/logs); both-ends-agreeing vectors prove cross-equality never counts |\n12151|| destination_host_id | independent invocation fact (per endpoint) | Attach: each end null (no destination argument); logs: each end equals the actual explicit --peer host per-endpoint; both-agreeing vectors prove cross-equality never counts |\n12152|| expectation_digest | endpoint-local observation | Digest binding action expectations; plan equals current via revalidate; per-row vectors |\n12153|\n12154|Synthetic digests are never independently recomputed to manufacture authority:\n12155|endpoint-local digest/lease/authority/expectation facts are validated by\n12156|plan/current equality (revalidate) at every applicable boundary plus receiver\n12157|expected admission, with per-row changed/missing witnesses. Temporal execution\n12158|(that a retry/resume actually re-ran) is a runtime prerequisite outside this\n12159|source evaluator. The denominator is closed at 159 divergence witnesses derived\n12160|directly from the 26-row composed context inventory joined with the member\n12161|disposition above: every applicable independent fact at every source-derived\n12162|composed route/endpoint/boundary/scope context, per endpoint, plus\n12163|both-ends-agreeing vectors for action/destination at every such context (and\n12164|initiator selection agreement vectors where both ends wrong still refuse via\n12165|the initiator check). Pre-effect, fencing and projection boundaries carry their\n12166|own invocation-binding witnesses with the context boundary set to pre-effect,\n12167|fencing or projection; plan/current revalidation alone cannot substitute for\n12168|this binding because two agreeing copies of a wrong plan never prove the actual\n12169|invocation. Invocation binding is checked unconditionally at every applicable\n12170|dispatch, admission, pre-effect, fencing, projection, retry and resume point,\n12171|so single-context narrowing at any one point is detected while all other points\n12172|still check.\n12173|\n12174|| Composed route | Plan side | Scope | Invocation fact | Plan field | Required relation | Divergence witness |\n12175|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n12176|| attach | initiator | initial | route attach | action | equals attach | <code>SEL-CASE-remote-initiator-action-mismatch</code> |\n12177|| attach | initiator | initial | no destination argument | destination_host_id | is null | <code>SEL-CASE-remote-initiator-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12178|| attach | initiator | initial | literal invocation selector | selector | equals selection.selector | <code>SEL-CASE-remote-initiator-selector-mismatch</code> |\n12179|| attach | initiator | initial | alias of selected source | source_alias | equals selected source alias (null for local) | <code>SEL-CASE-remote-initiator-alias-mismatch</code> |\n12180|| attach | initiator | initial | resolved session UUID | session_id | equals resolved session_id | <code>SEL-CASE-remote-initiator-session-mismatch</code> |\n12181|| attach | initiator | initial | resolved record digest | session_record_id | equals resolved session_record_id | <code>SEL-CASE-remote-initiator-record-mismatch</code> |\n12182|| attach | initiator | initial | resolved source host | source_host_id | equals resolved source_host_id | <code>SEL-CASE-remote-initiator-source-mismatch</code> |\n12183|| attach | initiator | initial-retry | route attach | action | equals attach | <code>SEL-CASE-remote-retry-initiator-action-mismatch</code> |\n12184|| attach | i