{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c75f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08841-b416-7e52-96f7-950fb1e6ed56"},"sequence":522,"recorded_at":1780531400001039,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08842-9e24-7231-9db8-f09013f68239"},"task_id":"01a08842-9e24-7231-9db8-f09013f68239","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08842-9e24-7231-9db8-f09013f68239","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`.\n(239 line(s) above)\n240|\tRecordID   string\n241|\tName       string\n242|\tKind       string\n243|\tProviderID string\n244|}\n245|\n246|// Event is one decoded authoritative Session Event: the routing\n247|// members plus the closed payload object admitted by the canonical\n248|// owner at decode time.\n249|type Event struct {\n250|\tID              string\n251|\tType            string\n252|\tSchemaVersion   string\n253|\tSessionID       string\n254|\tCreatedByHostID string\n255|\tLeaseEpoch      uint64\n256|\tLeaseID         string\n257|\tSequence        uint64\n258|\tPredecessors    []string\n259|\tPayload         map[string]any\n260|}\n261|\n262|// Input is the complete pure-reducer input: the record, the\n263|// authoritative events in chain order, the competing off-chain leases\n264|// observed at union, the lease the local host acts under (zero when\n265|// unknown), the local host ID (empty when unknown), and the parked\n266|// channel (non-nil when sessrepo reports the session parked).\n267|type Input struct {\n268|\tRecord      Record\n269|\tEvents      []Event\n270|\tUnion       []LeaseHead\n271|\tLocal       LeaseHead\n272|\tLocalHostID string\n273|\tParked      *ParkedFacts\n274|}\n275|\n276|// Projection is the derived session surface: lifecycle state, winning\n277|// lease, conflicts, current checkpoint, provider identity, terminal\n278|// binding, owner and role, the parked channel when set, and warnings.\n279|type Projection struct {\n280|\tSessionID     string\n281|\tRecordID      string\n282|\tName          string\n283|\tKind          string\n284|\tState         State\n285|\tWinner        LeaseHead\n286|\tConflicts     []Conflict\n287|\tHasCheckpoint bool\n288|\tNewest        Checkpoint\n289|\tProvider      ProviderIdentity\n290|\tHasTerminal   bool\n291|\tTerminal      TerminalBinding\n292|\tOwnerHostID   string\n293|\tLocalRole     string\n294|\tParked        *ParkedFacts\n295|\tWarnings      []string\n296|}\n297|\n298|// Reduce folds one record with its authoritative events into a\n299|// Projection. It is pure: no I/O, no clock, no cache. Chain continuity\n300|// is re-checked over the input, so a chain-forbidden reordering\n301|// refuses with invalid_state_transition instead of silently deriving a\n302|// different state.\n303|func Reduce(input Input) (Projection, error) {\n304|\tprojection := Projection{\n305|\t\tSessionID: input.Record.SessionID,\n306|\t\tRecordID:  input.Record.RecordID,\n307|\t\tName:      input.Record.Name,\n308|\t\tKind:      input.Record.Kind,\n309|\t\tProvider:  ProviderIdentity{ID: input.Record.ProviderID},\n310|\t}\n311|\tif input.Parked != nil {\n312|\t\tprojection.State = StateParked\n313|\t\tprojection.Parked = &ParkedFacts{\n314|\t\t\tBlockingReason: input.Parked.BlockingReason,\n315|\t\t\tRetryHint:      input.Parked.RetryHint,\n316|\t\t}\n317|\t\tprojection.Warnings = []string{\"parked: \" + input.Parked.BlockingReason}\n318|\t\treturn projection, nil\n319|\t}\n320|\tif input.Record.SessionID == \"\" || input.Record.RecordID == \"\" {\n321|\t\treturn Projection{}, refuse(ErrInvalidRecord, \"reducer input carries no session identity\")\n322|\t}\n323|\tfold := &chainFold{\n324|\t\trecordID:       input.Record.RecordID,\n325|\t\trecordProvider: input.Record.ProviderID,\n326|\t\tprojection:     &projection,\n327|\t}\n328|\tfor index := range input.Events {\n329|\t\tif err := fold.apply(input.Events[index]); err != nil {\n330|\t\t\treturn Projection{}, err\n331|\t\t}\n332|\t}\n333|\tif len(input.Events) == 0 {\n334|\t\t// An empty chain derives creating, but the union still\n335|\t\t// passes through resolveWinner below: a malformed union\n336|\t\t// refuses here exactly as on a non-empty chain, and a\n337|\t\t// well-formed union moves only the reported winner while\n338|\t\t// authoritative state stays creating.\n339|\t\tfold.state = StateCreating\n340|\t}\n341|\tif err := fold.resolveWinner(input.Union); err != nil {\n342|\t\treturn Projection{}, err\n343|\t}\n344|\tfold.applyLocalLease(input.Local, input.LocalHostID)\n345|\tfold.emitWarnings()\n346|\treturn projection, nil\n347|}\n348|\n349|// chainFold carries the mutable fold state across one Reduce call. It\n350|// never escapes Reduce.\n351|type chainFold struct {\n352|\trecordID       string\n353|\trecordProvider string\n354|\tprojection     *Projection\n355|\tstate          State\n356|\tcurrent        LeaseHead\n357|\tcreateLease    LeaseHead\n358|\thaveLease      bool\n359|\tseenCheckpoint bool\n360|\tseenAbort      bool\n361|\tonChain        map[string]struct{}\n362|\ttailID         string\n363|\ttailSeq        uint64\n364|\tleases         []LeaseHead\n365|\tprevious       LeaseHead\n366|}\n367|\n368|// apply folds one event: continuity first, then the type effect.\n369|func (fold *chainFold) apply(event Event) error {\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
