tracked `.task-board` files; after, 19\n22|  deletions + 3 modifications remain, all non-JSON board-checkout\n23|  artifacts (activity streams, progress/README markdown), none of them\n24|  product files and none covered by a validation gate.\n25|- Exact failed gate re-run on the final candidate:\n26|  `git ls-files -z '*.json' | xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c\n27|  'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'` → exit 0\n28|  (122 tracked JSON files, all parse).\n29|- Product bytes untouched: zero product edits in this run. The working\n30|  candidate is exactly the RUN-260909-bd27d9 candidate: tracked delta\n31|  `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`, `internal/sessrepo/store.go`,\n32|  `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo_test.go`; untracked `internal/sessquery/`\n33|  (13 files). sha256 (abbrev): LOGBOOK `da0823d6`, README `86af5b32`,\n34|  store.go `28d64e24`, sessrepo_test.go `a5618be2`, query.go `bde3c9c8`,\n35|  selector.go `6769455f`, plan.go `eaa82f3a`, revalidate.go `818df82e`,\n36|  digest.go `b6cc6a27`, TRACEABILITY.md `0fde2779`.\n37|- No stray `--help/` tree at the worktree root (verified absent); the\n38|  preserved prior-run artifact stays under gitignored\n39|  `.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/stray/` and is not in the candidate diff.\n40|\n41|## 2. Validation re-derived by this run on the final candidate (real exits)\n42|\n43|| Command | Exit |\n44|| --- | --- |\n45|| `go build ./...` | 0 |\n46|| `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n47|| `gofmt -l internal/sessquery/ internal/sessrepo/` (empty) | 0 |\n48|| `git diff --check -- internal/ LOGBOOK.md README.md` | 0 |\n49|| `go test ./... -count=1` (all 26 packages ok) | 0 |\n50|| `go test ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessstate/ -cover` (91.0% / 87.6% / 92.2%) | 0 |\n51|| `go test ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessstate/ -race -count=1` | 0 |\n52|| tracked-JSON gate above | 0 |\n53|\n54|Raw logs: `TASK-260830-21gygk_validation-ffb76b.log` (attached).\n55|\n56|## 3. Mutation evidence (reused exact-cand