{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08841-b416-7e52-96f7-950fb1e6ed56"},"sequence":715,"recorded_at":1780531400001425,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08844-6103-7802-90a6-49f576e75e9f"},"task_id":"01a08844-6103-7802-90a6-49f576e75e9f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08844-6103-7802-90a6-49f576e75e9f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-13-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls internal/sessadapter/; grep -rn \\\"lease\\\" internal/sessadapter/*.go | grep -v _test | head -n 20; echo ===; grep -n \\\"5\\\\.3\\\\|5\\\\.7\\\\|Lease Record\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Check sessadapter and spec lease sections\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"bound_census_test.go\\nbounds_edge_test.go\\ncensus_test.go\\ncontext.go\\ncontext_test.go\\ndecode.go\\ndiscovery.go\\ndiscovery_test.go\\ndoc.go\\nenvelope_test.go\\nfixtures_test.go\\nidentity_census_test.go\\nimport_census_test.go\\ninventory_test.go\\ninventory_witnesses_test.go\\nmanifest.go\\nmanifest_test.go\\noperations.go\\noperations_derived_test.go\\noperations_semantic_test.go\\noperations_test.go\\nprobe.go\\nprobe_test.go\\nprotocol.go\\nrawuint53_test.go\\nsurrogate_test.go\\ntuple.go\\ntuple_test.go\\nzero_absent_test.go\\n===\\n1004:to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\\n1338:codes, exit classes, and bootstrap behavior are defined in Section 15.3. These\\n1908:### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\\n1910:The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\\n1915:| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\\n1917:| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\\n2284:### 5.7 Derived session states\\n4283:Section 5.7 state engine using the active ax transition: bridge\\n7271:| <code>handoff.commit</code> | Persist the destination Lease Record on the source and park the old owner |\\n7387:| <code>lease.refresh</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,known_lease_record_ids:sorted unique digest[0..4096]}</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,missing_leases:sorted unique Lease Record[0..4096],winner:LeaseHead,divergence:boolean}</code> |\\n7394:| <code>handoff.commit</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,new_lease:Lease Record,destination_materialization_id:UUIDv7,plan_id:digest,committed_checkpoint_id:digest}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,winner:LeaseHead,source_role:replica,source_state:parked}</code> |\\n7574:lease to the source. It MUST validate the complete Lease Record, require the\\n7587:| Session Record, Lease Record, Checkpoint Record, Workspace Group Record, Provider Identity Record | Respective <code>record_id</code> or <code>checkpoint_id</code> | <code>record</code> |\\n7743:5. lease heads are derived after union using Section 5.3;\\n9014:   that group, the initial Lease Record, and <code>session.created</code> carrying\\n9244:input. The initiating host remains a replica. No Lease Record, workspace\\n9325:   destination union and persist that Lease Record. Destination MUST verify it\\n11952:| <code>lease_record_id</code> | Validated winning Lease Record digest |\\n11987:covers every Section 5.3 fencing check, `commit` precedes durable publication,\\n11991:interruption under Section 5.3. None may skip checks because a previous phase\\n12355:validated winning Lease Record, including the initial epoch-1 create lease.\\n12407:initial_lease (the complete allocated Lease Record 1.0.0 described by the\\n12432:unknown members are refused. Its embedded Lease Record retains every required\\n12433:Section 5.3 member, including nullable members, canonical self digest,\\n14835:### 15.3 Stable error codes\\n15916:| Attach, takeover, failure, and fork | Sections 5.3–5.7, 13, 14, 15, 16.5, 19.4 |\\n15940:| Exactly one owner, epoch fencing, replicas | Sections 2.2, 5.3, 11.4, 13.6–13.7, AC-OWN cases |\\n15951:| Approved v0.4.3 roadmap and macOS terminal-realm boundaries | Sections 2.2–2.3, 3.1–3.2, 4.2/4.4, 7.1, 12.1–12.3, 13.3/13.5–13.6/13.11/13.15, 14.1, 15.3, 16.2, 17.1, 19.1–19.4, and Appendix D |\\n15959:| Canonical state and destination enums | SessionState in Section 5.7, explicit task-board mapping in Section 9.2, DestinationClass in Sections 11.3 and 11.7, and their RPC/CLI reuse |\\n15997:| Epoch-1 failed launch had no stop/resume representation | Sections 5.2, 5.7, 11.3, 13.1–13.2, 13.9–13.10, and 14.2 define bootstrap retry/abort, nullable checkpoint, non-resumable failed state, and exact RPC/Event/CLI agreement; <code>AC-BOOT-001</code> covers every boundary |\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3790,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 948,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
