{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c91f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08841-b416-7e52-96f7-950fb1e6ed56"},"sequence":746,"recorded_at":1780531400001487,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08844-6f0d-7572-95e0-b631a4a77b6f"},"task_id":"01a08844-6f0d-7572-95e0-b631a4a77b6f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08844-6f0d-7572-95e0-b631a4a77b6f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1907 line(s) above)\n1908|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1909|\n1910|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1911|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1912|\n1913|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1914|| --- | --- | --- |\n1915|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1916|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1917|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\n1918|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1919|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\n1920|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\n1921|| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\n1922|| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\n1923|| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\n1924|| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\n1925|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\n1926|| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\n1927|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\n1928|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n1929|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1930|\n1931|The object is closed; every row is required, including nullable fields.\n1932|Normative example:\n1933|\n1934|~~~json\n1935|{\n1936|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:lease\",\n1937|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1938|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:8ead987abed8c7c05175b447c9a0e2b3a521f12e5a989acb8abe132576852d63\",\n1939|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1940|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1941|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1942|  \"epoch\": 4,\n1943|  \"holder_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1944|  \"predecessor_lease_id\": \"bbbbbbbb-cccc-4ddd-8eee-ffffffffffff\",\n1945|  \"reason\": \"graceful_takeover\",\n1946|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1947|  \"issued_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1948|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n1949|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:00.000Z\",\n1950|  \"extensions\": {}\n1951|}\n1952|~~~\n1953|\n1954|The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\n1955|<code>(epoch, lease_id)</code>, where <code>lease_id</code> uses bytewise UUID\n1956|order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\n1957|tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the\n1958|same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference\n1959|a validated checkpoint for that session and predecessor lease. An epoch-1\n1960|<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null\n1961|checkpoint before the first provider boundary exists. Every new takeover lease\n1962|MUST use <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code> from the initiator's current union.\n1963|\n1964|The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\n1965|clock ordering. Both processes can temporarily continue in isolated partitions,\n1966|which is why force takeover warns about split brain. After union, exactly one\n1967|lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST\n1968|be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.\n1969|\n1970|An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:\n1971|\n1972|- accepting operator input after attach;\n1973|- starting a provider turn;\n1974|- publishing a checkpoint;\n1975|- pushing records or workspace changes; and\n1976|- resuming after any transport or sleep interruption longer than the configured\n1977|  lease refresh interval.\n1978|\n1979|There is no time-expiring ownership lease in v0.5.0. Liveness is not authority.\n1980|A host being offline does not make a replica owner; only a takeover or fork\n1981|does.\n1982|\n1983|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n1984|\n1985|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n1986|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n1987|\n1988|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1989|| --- | --- | --- |\n1990|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Checkpoint schema identifier |\n1991|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1992|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1993|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1994|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing Session Record |\n1995|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero and equal to the referenced winning lease |\n1996|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Equal to that lease's fencing token |\n1997|| <code>safe_boundary</code> | Safe Boundary Evidence | Closed shape below |\n1998|| <code>event_heads</code> | sorted unique digest[1..64] | Authoritative event DAG heads immediately before this object |\n1999|| <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Workspace-group Transfer Manifest root |\n2000|| <code>provider_manifest_id</code> | digest or null | Direct native-store/provider snapshot only |\n2001|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Task-board path only |\n2002|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Current lease holder |\n2003|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2004|| <code>status</code> | enum | Literal <code>validated</code> |\n2005|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2006|\n2007|Safe Boundary Evidence is a closed object containing exactly\n2008|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n2009|<code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>,\n2010|<code>evidence:provider_api|provider_event|managed_pty|task_board_bridge|accepted_test</code>,\n2011|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n2012|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, and\n2013|<code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>. A published checkpoint requires all\n2014|three booleans true and both counters zero. Provider-specific scheduled or\n2015|child work is included in <code>background_idle</code> and\n2016|<code>open_processes</code>; an adapter that cannot prove it MUST NOT publish a\n2017|new checkpoint.\n2018|\n2019|The referenced Session Record selects the persistence variant. For\n2020|<code>kind = direct</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be non-null\n2021|and <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be null. A backend-resolved provider\n2022|with no portable bytes still uses a provider Transfer Manifest containing its\n2023|validated identity and zero file entries; null is not used to erase that\n2024|distinction. For <code>kind = task_board</code>,\n2025|<code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be null and\n2026|<code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be non-null. Both-null and both-non-null\n2027|checkpoints are invalid.\n2028|\n2029|A checkpoint MUST NOT be published until every referenced object exists,\n2030|hashes correctly, passes schema validation, and the provider/task-board path\n2031|meets its quiescence requirement. A force takeover MAY select the newest\n2032|validated checkpoint even when no new safe checkpoint can be created.\n2033|\n2034|<code>event_heads</code> identifies the authoritative event DAG immediately\n2035|before the checkpoint object. A later <code>checkpoint.created</code> event MAY\n2036|reference that checkpoint and those heads; the checkpoint MUST NOT reference\n2037|the announcing event because that would create a circular digest dependency.\n2038|The transitive event-head closure also fixes the Section 2.4 effective\n2039|execution profile and its nullable source event for this checkpoint. A missing,\n2040|losing-lease, or non-newest <code>profile.changed</code> reference is\n2041|<code>integrity_failure</code>; checkpoint consumers MUST NOT consult a later\n2042|local-only profile event or fall back to the creation profile.\n2043|\n2044|Normative negative fixtures are: <code>CP-N1</code>, with\n2045|<code>background_idle = false</code> and status <code>validated</code>;\n2046|<code>CP-N2</code>, with a direct Session Record and null provider manifest;\n2047|<code>CP-N3</code>, with both persistence IDs non-null; and\n2048|<code>CP-N4</code>, with an unknown <code>safe_boundary.pid</code> member. Each\n2049|MUST be rejected with <code>incompatible_schema</code> before publication.\n2050|\n2051|Normative example:\n2052|\n2053|~~~json\n2054|{\n2055|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\",\n2056|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2057|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2058|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2059|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2060|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n2061|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2062|  \"safe_boundary\": {\n2063|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n2064|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n2065|    \"evidence\": \"accepted_test\",\n2066|    \"input_blocked\": true,\n2067|    \"foreground_idle\": true,\n2068|    \"background_idle\": true,\n2069|    \"open_processes\": 0,\n2070|    \"open_database_handles\": 0\n2071|  },\n2072|  \"event_heads\": [\n2073|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n2074|  ],\n2075|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n2076|  \"provider_manifest_id\": \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n2077|  \"task_board_bundle_id\": null,\n2078|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2079|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:30.000Z\",\n2080|  \"status\": \"validated\",\n2081|  \"extensions\": {}\n2082|}\n2083|~~~\n2084|\n2085|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2086|\n2087|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c921","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08841-b416-7e52-96f7-950fb1e6ed56"},"sequence":747,"recorded_at":1780531400001489,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08844-6f0d-7572-95e0-b631a4a77b6f"},"task_id":"01a08844-6f0d-7572-95e0-b631a4a77b6f","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a08844-6f0d-7572-95e0-b631a4a77b6f"}}}
