{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca11","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08841-b416-7e52-96f7-950fb1e6ed56"},"sequence":867,"recorded_at":1780531400001729,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"82802766-dfb1-4d49-b692-3924c0687d9f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08846-577d-7511-bcb6-e941027b1683"},"task_id":"01a08846-577d-7511-bcb6-e941027b1683","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08846-577d-7511-bcb6-e941027b1683","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1832 line(s) above)\n1833|## Session selector, read summaries, and selection plans\n1834|\n1835|`internal/sessquery` is the single shared selector API over the persisted\n1836|session repositories and the accepted state projector. It implements the\n1837|v0.6.0 selector contract (§14.7/§14.7.1, refining §2.3) with shared\n1838|SelectionPlan construction and revalidation (§14.7.2):\n1839|\n1840|- Literal grammar: split at the first `@` only. The key is a NAME, a bare\n1841|  UUID (name-first precedence kept), or `id:UUID` (bypasses names for the\n1842|  durable union identity). The source is empty (bare §2.3 tiers), `local`,\n1843|  `peer:ALIAS` (the entire remaining suffix, literal — spaces, `@`,\n1844|  Unicode, and `%` included), or `id:HOST_UUID`. No joining, aliasing,\n1845|  percent-decoding, Unicode normalization, trimming, or alias folding.\n1846|- Exact source mappings: effective configuration (local host, peer\n1847|  alias/host mappings, allowlist) is validated first, including exact\n1848|  alias and host-ID uniqueness; duplicates are `invalid_config`.\n1849|  Explicit unknown aliases/hosts are `selector_source_not_found`; known\n1850|  but disallowed peers are `peer_not_allowlisted`. Remote read failures\n1851|  are `selector_source_read_failed` with the cause preserved; local I/O\n1852|  keeps its repository error; malformed authority is `integrity_failure`.\n1853|- No explicit-source fallback: a qualified key resolves in its one\n1854|  source only. Tier, collision, and tombstone semantics follow §14.7.1:\n1855|  exact live name then UUID-shaped name within the source, replicated\n1856|  copies deduplicate only on agreeing record digests (else\n1857|  `integrity_failure`), distinct colliding names refuse with\n1858|  `name_ambiguous`, and tombstoned entries stay excluded on\n1859|  authoritative tombstone evidence while failed reads never count as it.\n1860|- Immutable plans: `Reader.BuildPlan` binds the literal selector,\n1861|  session and validated record digest, source host and exact alias,\n1862|  index and configuration digests, winning lease triple, event-head\n1863|  authority heads, action, destination, and expectation digest.\n1864|  `Reader.Revalidate` compares every bound fact in a fixed order at any\n1865|  boundary in `BoundariesFor`; divergence is `selector_plan_stale`,\n1866|  revocation is `peer_not_allowlisted`, and reads keep their classes.\n1867|  Plans authorize read projection only; fencing, commit, and remote\n1868|  routes belong to the CLI/lifecycle callers that invoke revalidation.\n1869|\n1870|`Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` read actual Session Records and event\n1871|chains through `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the\n1872|derived identity, provider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role,\n1873|checkpoint ID, conflicts, and warnings as an internal `Summary`. List\n1874|order is bytewise session ID; `InspectLocal` retains access to\n1875|parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics. Failed index reads and\n1876|failed projections propagate as errors. Repository-parked sessions\n1877|remain visible in listing but are excluded from live routing. Reading\n1878|never repairs a store or performs an attach, resume, or ownership\n1879|change. A record without any valid lease keeps the accepted internal\n1880|projection with empty owner/lease facts: creating is a record AND an\n1881|authoritative initial lease (§5.7/§13.1 step 2), so a record-only chain\n1882|is an interrupted prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf, never a\n1883|public creating claim and never a placeholder owner.\n1884|\n1885|These entries do not provide an `ax` executable or a closed CLI Result\n1886|renderer. CLI Result 5 with Structured Error 1.4.0, wire exit binding,\n1887|lease-record objects, observation contracts, transports, peer\n1888|authentication, and lifecycle effects belong to their owning leaves.\n1889|`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` drives `Reader.List`\n1890|and the existing `cliresult.New` to demonstrate that a creating session\n1891|without owner facts cannot satisfy the mandatory CLI owner/lease\n1892|fields. No owner is invented and no doctor/provider/platform capability\n1893|is advertised. The traceability, gate battery, and remaining bounds are\n1894|in [the task evidence map](internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md).\n1895|\n1896|```bash\n1897|go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo -count=1 -v\n1898|python3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\n1899|```\n1900|\n1901|## Structured Errors, Stable Codes, and Causal Redaction\n1902|\n1903|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) implements the Section 15 Structured\n1904|Error contract: the closed versioned failure object, its stable code-to-exit\n1905|registry, its retryability rule, its typed diagnostic details, and the redaction\n1906|that keeps a local cause off the wire. The package holds no state, opens no\n1907|file, starts no process, and mutates nothing durable, so it has no crash or\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
